discovery:
Sulfur has been known since ancient times (Egypt, Greece). In 1777, Lavoisier established it was a chemical
            element. Pure sulfur isolated by Gay‑Lussac and Thénard in early 1800s.
            :contentReference[oaicite:7]{index=7}

didYouKnow:
The Biblical term “brimstone” refers to sulfur. Ancient Egyptians used it in ointments over 4,000 years ago.
            Sulfuric acid remains one of the most widely produced industrial chemicals.
            :contentReference[oaicite:11]{index=11}
